  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Secondary School Scholarships Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Secondary School Scholarships Program (PSSSP) aimed to prepare students from Pacific island countries for leadership through secondary education scholarships. The program was paused in 2020 in response to the COVID-19 pandemic and before any students arrived. With Australian migration reforms (Pacific Engagement Visa and PALM family accompaniment) establishing new pathways for Pacific students to study at Australian secondary schools, a decision was made not to recommence the program and it was terminated in June 2023. Program funds were instead provided to the World Bank to undertake research and pilot interventions to lift the performance of secondary schools in four countries (Fiji, Kiribati, Tonga, RMI). This program continues to be implemented.</narrative>
  </description>
